.TH MINCORE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
mincore \- query memory residency
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/mman.h>
.B int mincore(void* address, size_t byte_count, unsigned char* vector);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes one byte per page in the page\-aligned range. The low bit indicates
whether that page was resident at the instant of the query. The writable
vector must contain at least ceil(byte_count / page size) bytes.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mincore (2)
